 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "H1",
   "t0": 0.238,
   "t1": 2.312,
   "text": "Five real heists that sound made up.",
   "kind": "hook",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E5.0",
   "t0": 2.912,
   "t1": 3.722,
   "text": "Number five.",
   "kind": "announce",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E5.1",
   "t0": 4.227,
   "t1": 11.444,
   "text": "In 2024, a scammer posing as a French distributor ordered 22 tonnes of artisan cheddar from a London dairy.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E5.2",
   "t0": 11.71,
   "t1": 15.677,
   "text": "950 wheels, worth about 300,000 pounds.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E5.3",
   "t0": 15.944,
   "t1": 18.369,
   "text": "The dairy delivered. The money never came.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E4.0",
   "t0": 19.016,
   "t1": 19.76,
   "text": "Number four.",
   "kind": "announce",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E4.1",
   "t0": 20.265,
   "t1": 25.624,
   "text": "In 1911, a former Louvre worker tucked the Mona Lisa under his smock and walked out.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E4.2",
   "t0": 25.89,
   "t1": 29.457,
   "text": "Nobody noticed for a day. Police even questioned Picasso.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E4.3",
   "t0": 29.724,
   "t1": 32.213,
   "text": "It surfaced two years later, in Florence.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E3.0",
   "t0": 32.861,
   "t1": 33.562,
   "text": "Number three.",
   "kind": "announce",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E3.1",
   "t0": 34.067,
   "t1": 39.829,
   "text": "In 2003, a crew beat 10 layers of security and took over 100 million in diamonds.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E3.2",
   "t0": 40.095,
   "t1": 42.162,
   "text": "Then they dumped their trash in a forest.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E3.3",
   "t0": 42.429,
   "t1": 45.454,
   "text": "A half-eaten sandwich with the leader's DNA got him caught.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.0",
   "t0": 46.102,
   "t1": 46.783,
   "text": "Number two.",
   "kind": "announce",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.1",
   "t0": 47.288,
   "t1": 55.11,
   "text": "In 1968, a fake motorcycle cop stopped a bank car in Tokyo, lit a road flare under it, and yelled bomb.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.2",
   "t0": 55.377,
   "t1": 59.352,
   "text": "The guards ran. He drove off with 294 million yen.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.3",
   "t0": 59.619,
   "t1": 60.314,
   "text": "Never caught.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.0",
   "t0": 61.01,
   "t1": 61.716,
   "text": "Number one.",
   "kind": "announce",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.1",
   "t0": 62.221,
   "t1": 70.743,
   "text": "In 2012, thieves drained 9,500 barrels of maple syrup, worth 18 million dollars, from Canada's strategic reserve.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.2",
   "t0": 71.01,
   "t1": 72.503,
   "text": "Yes, that exists.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.3",
   "t0": 72.77,
   "t1": 74.43,
   "text": "They refilled the barrels with water.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.4",
   "t0": 74.697,
   "t1": 78.223,
   "text": "An auditor only noticed when he climbed a barrel, and nearly fell in.",
   "kind": "entry",
   "mismatch": false
  },
  {
   "id": "O1",
   "t0": 78.937,
   "t1": 80.569,
   "text": "Which one would you have pulled off?",
   "kind": "outro",
   "mismatch": false
  }
 ],
